  "$schema": "../gen/schemas/desktop-schema.json",
  "identifier": "user-apps",
  "description": "What every window may do — user-provided web apps and the system apps (Notes...) alike, they have the same rights: use files under the user folder and folders the user picks with a native folder picker (the fs_* commands, which obey the app's own scope: the user folder plus picked folders, minus the app's own data), SQLite databases in those same places, the Filen.io accounts the user has connected (file operations only — never credentials), manage app windows, tab groups, tabs and their tags, open a file or a note as a web app and tell the windows that show a file that it was saved (the Notes commands), and export a file to the device (a native 'save as' dialog on desktop, a confirmation before writing to Downloads on Android — every time). Deliberately absent (the admin-app's, see admin.json): connecting/disconnecting Filen accounts, data-folder management, real paths, system/OS information, and window/app introspection. Yes/no questions are asked with confirm_dialog (a native box under the prompt rules of docs/app-security.md), not with the dialog plugin, whose commands are the admin-app's.",
  "windows": [
    "*"
  ],
